{"full":"hf:lvwerra/cowrite","spaceId":"lvwerra/cowrite","name":"cowrite","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":5,"created":"2026-07-16T21:18:51.000Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:10:29.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://lvwerra-cowrite.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/cowrite","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:03:56.761Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:03:56.761Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:03:56.761Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"✍️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A real-time collaborative document editor (Google-Docs-lite) where AI agents are collaborators that never write directly — they only:","Agents are invoked from comments: mention @your-agent do something and the task is delivered to the agent the next time it polls. The comment shows a live status chip: ⏳ pending → 👀 seen → ✅ handled (or ⚠️ failed). Each user brings their own agent (Claude Code, Codex, …) — the UI has a \"copy agent prompt\" button that turns any coding agent into a polling collaborator. Signed-in users also get a private built-in OpenCode worker powered by moonshotai/Kimi-K3 through Hugging Face Inference Providers. Its only enabled network tool is web search; Cowrite validates and applies its structured…","The agent prompt is explicit about where an agent's output goes: the document is the deliverable, so anything worth reading later is proposed as a suggestion or a new page, and thread replies stay one or two sentences (\"what I did, where to look\"). Overlong comments are collapsed behind a \"Show more\" in the UI."],"features":["comment in anchored threads, and","propose suggestions (block replacements) that a human accepts or rejects."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/cowrite/blob/main/README